@bio:

Wolfgang Drescher (born 1991 in Basel) completed a
master’s degree in music theory with Prof. Dr. Felix
Diergarten at the Freiburg University of Music in 2018.
From 2018–2021 he worked as a programmer and project
manager at jkweb in Basel and Zurich. After teaching as a
lecturer at the Freiburg University of Music, he became
professor of music theory with a focus on digital media at
the same university in 2021. His research develops
computational tools for music theory. He contributes to
open-source projects including Verovio and Humdrum and
co-developed “Singing upon the (Note-)book”
(contrapunto.ch).

@@END: BIO